    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσχᾰτ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be at the end,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐσχατεύοντα τῶν δένδρων</span> the
			parts <i>farthest off,</i> i.e. the branches, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				5.1.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.366b
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εύοντες τόποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					298a14
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>to be at the extremity,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς Ἀρκαδίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.77.8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be the lowest</i> or <i>meanest,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν διδασκόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					2.54S.
				</span></i>
			</div>
